// C11 6.5: after a complete operand only an operator can continue an
// expression. madc's engine read on past a juxtaposed operand and let a LATER
// operator bind the pair: `int x = 3 4 +;` built `3 + 4` and exited 7. The
// engine now ends the expression before the `4` (Program::parseExpression,
// token_begins_operand) and the declaration reports what it needed there.
// Oracle: gcc "error: expected ',' or ';' before numeric constant", clang
// "error: expected ';' at end of declaration".
int main(void) { int x = 3 4 +; return x; }
